cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Octet dimer-tetramer model: two-step kinetic analysis of Eph / ephrin-Fc biolayer interferometry"
abstract: >-
  Kinetic analysis of Octet biolayer-interferometry sensorgrams for Eph receptor
  binding to Fc-dimerized ephrin ligands with a two-step heterodimer to
  heterotetramer model: global biexponential dissociation fits, a global
  two-phase association fit with profiled rate slopes, window-aware flags, and
  within-protocol WT vs mutant statistics.
authors:
  - family-names: Khambete
    given-names: Amav
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: MIT
keywords:
  - biolayer interferometry
  - binding kinetics
  - Eph receptor
  - ephrin
  - tetramerization
